  "supply_chain_lifecycle": {
    "states": ["DEFERRED", "QUALIFIED_NOT_ACTIVE", "EVIDENCE_ONLY", "ACTIVE"],
    "DEFERRED": "Default. The component may not appear in executable source, imports, production manifests, build files, images or runtime configuration. A protected CONTRACT_ONLY protocol manifest may name it only as a non-activating wire contract; the architecture checker rejects runtime references, capabilities and activation from that surface. Its leak-scan tokens are denied repository-wide.",
    "QUALIFIED_NOT_ACTIVE": "The component has passed exact-version qualification and may be used ONLY inside its declared isolated worker build/test subtree. It stays unreachable from production composition, deploy and runtime: no application source in the subtree, no production manifest referencing it, no production image build context containing it, no direct application import. Its leak-scan tokens stay denied everywhere outside that subtree — this is a narrowing of scope, not a suspension of the scan.",
    "EVIDENCE_ONLY": "Real build or test evidence exists, but one or more release gates are still red (such as reproducibility, vulnerability, offline provenance or the production v2 wire). The component is permitted only inside its declared isolated evidence subtree, remains unreachable from production, and cannot be called an acceptance or activation proof.",
    "ACTIVE": "Production use is permitted. A component reaches ACTIVE only atomically with a working end-to-end path and acceptance evidence, and leaving QUALIFIED_NOT_ACTIVE or EVIDENCE_ONLY requires editing both this lock and the closed registry in scripts/check-architecture.go, so activation cannot be a silent or forgotten step.",
    "rule": "Every deferred entry declares its lifecycle explicitly; there is no implicit state. A QUALIFIED_NOT_ACTIVE or EVIDENCE_ONLY entry must additionally declare its exact version, isolated subtree, exact leak tokens and evidence document. A CONTRACT_ONLY protocol manifest is not an executable production surface and must pass its dedicated no-activation check. The boundary is enforced by checkSupplyChainLifecycleBoundary, checkDeploymentManifests and checkDeferredStageLeaks, and is reusable per component without copying an exception."
  },
